    "Uncertain provisioning health refuses before baseline, and stored intent/receipt is revalidated against the immutable adapter bundle",
    "Fleet alias reservation covers admission, execution and uncertain external recovery; alias URLs normalize trailing slashes exactly as HTTP transport does"
  ],
  "diagnostics": [
    "Independent review found a transport-equivalent trailing-slash alias bypass after the first full run had started. Fixed it, added unit/native refusal controls and reran full native and real-provider verification. Earlier evidence remains separately archived."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Provisioning uses configurable reachable HTTP/TLS adapters; no particular vendor or build fleet was selected. Native and dogfood external mutations stay inside disposable localhost fixtures.",
    "If the daemon records attempted but dies before sending, or the adapter cannot prove the effect, preparation stays uncertain and refuses automatic replay. No force-replay command is provided.",
    "Retirement is irreversible through this API; no adapter deletion, reactivation, executable installation or credential lifecycle is implemented.",
    "Fleet endpoint roles/grants and exact vendor schemas remain operator-configured. This implementation supplies protocol/orchestration, not vendor-specific fleet internals.",
    "Formal proofs cover the explicit production predicates and bounded synchronization/order models, not the HTTP server, database, Git, filesystem or provider internals."
  ],
